# Multiplayer Text-Based Network Game (C++ / Winsock2)

This project is a simple multiplayer text-based game built in C++ using Winsock2 and TCP networking. 
Multiple clients can connect to a central server, explore rooms, fight monsters, pick up items, 
and participate in a cooperative boss encounter. The server maintains all game state and uses 
a thread-per-client design to handle multiple simultaneous players.

The game world consists of multiple connected rooms, each containing descriptions, monsters, 
and items. Players interact with the world using text commands such as LOOK, MOVE, ATTACK, 
INVENTORY, and HELP. 

A special boss command ("BOSS") teleports all connected players into a shared arena where they 
must work together to defeat a stronger enemy. The server broadcasts combat updates to all 
players in the boss room, tracks health, manages death states, and returns players to their 
original locations once the fight ends.

This project demonstrates fundamental socket programming, server-client communication, 
multi-threading, shared state management, and basic text-based game mechanics.

## How to Build

This project uses CMake. To compile:

1. Open a terminal inside the project folder.
2. Create and enter a build directory:

mkdir build
cd build

3. Configure the project with CMake:

cmake ..

4. Build the server and client executables:

cmake --build .


This will produce:

server.exe
client.exe

inside the build directory.

## How to Run

### Start the Server
In the build directory:

./server.exe


Leave this running.

### Start a Client
Open a second terminal (and more terminals for additional players):

./client.exe

Enter a username when prompted.


## Available Player Commands

LOOK
MOVE NORTH
MOVE SOUTH
MOVE EAST
MOVE WEST
ATTACK
PICKUP <item>
INVENTORY
HELP
SAY <message>
BOSS


- Movement changes the player’s position in the world.
- LOOK shows the room description, monsters, players, and items.
- ATTACK engages in combat with monsters or the boss.
- BOSS triggers a multiplayer boss fight event.